        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sedgebrook, Grantham, Lincolnshire, England, London King's Cross\n- Stations: Sedgebrook railway station, Grantham railway station\n- Railway lines: Nottingham to Grantham line, Ambergate, Nottingham, Boston and Eastern Junction Railway, East Coast Main Line\n\nFacts:\n- The Ambergate, Nottingham, Boston and Eastern Junction Railway opened on 15 July 1850.\n- Sedgebrook railway station was formerly a station on the Nottingham to Grantham line.\n- The Nottingham to Grantham line opened as the Ambergate, Nottingham, Boston and Eastern Junction Railway.\n- Grantham railway station serves the town of Grantham in Lincolnshire, England.\n- Grantham railway station lies on the East Coast Main Line 105.5 miles north of London King's Cross.",
